Package: com.iosvcam.opencam
Name: iOS-VCAM OpenCam
Version: 0.6.1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Open-source, editable virtual camera tweak. Runs in mediaserverd so it covers every capture client (stock Camera, TikTok, all apps). Pulls an RTMP stream on-device, decodes H264 via VideoToolbox, and overwrites the camera's OWN image buffer IN PLACE at BWNodeOutput -emitSampleBuffer: with a SINGLE GPU-accelerated VTPixelTransferSessionTransferImage (one pass, no per-frame pixel rotation, no CVPixelBuffer lock around the transfer), then passes the ORIGINAL sample buffer downstream - matching the closed vcamera's GPU sync discipline (render nodes stay pass-through; orientation is carried by the pipeline's existing metadata). Every landscape capture buffer is overwritten (landscape gate, no dedup, like the original); portrait buffers inherit OBS from the shared surface. The stock-Camera full-res still uses a separate 709 transfer session so the saved photo colour matches. Every client reads the same overwritten upstream IOSurface, so the app preview shows OBS. Fail-open everywhere (any error falls back to the real camera). NOTE: the microphone/audio hook (VCamAudioMS.x) is kept in the source tree but not compiled into this build - it returns with the upcoming OBS audio-replacement work. 0.6.0: MILESTONE CLEANUP of the device-verified 0.5.9 stable - identical runtime behaviour, but the settled freeze-hunt A/B diagnostics (VCAM_VIDEO_DEDUP, VCAM_PRIVATE_DEDUP_KEY, VCAM_GPU_FENCE_FLUSH, VCAM_STAMP_DEST) and the dead opt-in photo-node path (VCAM_HOOK_PHOTO_NODES, always deadlocked the GPU) are removed, leaving only the live emit-overwrite path the original actually uses. Dark-scene saved-photo red remains at parity with the closed vcamera (rendered by the iOS16 deferredmediad Deep Fusion daemon, outside mediaserverd's reach - see VCAMERA_OPENVCAM_COMPLETE_REFERENCE.md). 0.6.1: fix the stock-Camera Photo-mode preview cycling (clear->stutter->gaussian-blur every ~3s at the ZSL/Live-Photo queue restart). Root cause (RE, engine @0x82650): the rotation session was not GPU-accelerated - only the transfer session was - so the rotated buffer feeding the GPU transfer was not GPU-synced. Photo mode is the only mode using the rotation path (portrait OBS -> landscape dst; TikTok/portrait dst skips it and always worked), so its preview updated only at the ~3s restart. Fix: set EnableGPUAcceleratedTransfer on the rotation session too, and use NSRecursiveLock for the rotate+transfer critical section (engine @0x823f8), both matching the closed vcamera.
Maintainer: iOS-VCAM
Author: iOS-VCAM
Section: Tweaks
Depends: mobilesubstrate (>= 0.9.5000), network-cmds
Conflicts: com.x.vcamera, com.iosvcam.audiobridge, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.system-hook, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.media-active, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.media-probe, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.daemon, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.safe
Replaces: com.x.vcamera, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.media-active, com.iosvcam.audiobridge.safe
